+# Contract: MCP stdio surface — `tools/call` parameter validation
+
+**Feature**: specs/001-bench/spec.md · **Date**: 2026-10-26
+**Surface owner**: `task_handoff.py` (`--mcp-stdio` mode), byte-identical in both distributed copies.
+
+The adapter's external interface is newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout
+(MCP protocol version `2025-06-18`). This contract documents the wire behavior this feature
+changes — `tools/call` request validation — and pins the parts that must not move.
+
+## Framing (unchanged)
+
+- One JSON-RPC message per physical line on **stdin**; each reply one line on **stdout**, flushed,
+  compact-encoded (`separators=(",", ":")`), UTF-8.
+- A line longer than `MAX_MCP_MESSAGE` (32 768) bytes including its newline: reply
+  `{"id":null,"error":{"code":-32600,"message":"invalid request"}}` and **terminate**; remaining
+  bytes of the frame are never interpreted as further requests. (FR-006)
+
+## Unchanged methods (frozen for this feature)
+
+| Method | Behavior after change |
+|---|---|
+| `initialize` | Same `protocolVersion`, `capabilities`, `serverInfo` (`graphhelm-task-handoff`, version matching the plugin manifest). |
+| `ping` | Empty result `{}`. |
+| `tools/list` | Same three closed tools with identical schemas (`offer`, `receive`, `status`). |
+| Unknown method / notification handling | Identical to today. |
+
+## `tools/call` request — accepted shapes (post-change)
+
+Request:
+
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":N,"method":"tools/call",
+ "params":{"name":"<offer|receive|status>","arguments":{...},
+           "_meta":{"progressToken":"...","...any keys":"..."}}}
+```
+
+Accepted iff:
+
+1. `params` is an object;
+2. every key of `params` is one of `name`, `arguments`, `_meta`;
+3. if `_meta` is present it is an object;
+4. `name`/`arguments` pass the existing per-tool rules (unchanged).
+
+Success reply (dispatch happened; result semantics identical to the same call without `_meta`):
+
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":N,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<tool json>"}],"isError":false}}
+```
+
+Semantics of `_meta` (FR-001, FR-002): admitted but opaque — not used to select the tool, not
+merged into `arguments`, not consulted for identity, not included in the reply, not logged.
+Within the frame limit, any two calls differing only in `_meta` produce indistinguishable
+responses and identical Runtime traffic.
+
+## `tools/call` request — rejected shapes (all before dispatch, zero Runtime I/O)
+
+| Violation | Reply | Stage | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `params` missing or not an object | `{"id":N,"error":{"code":-32602,"message":"invalid request"}}` | param validation | unchanged |
+| `params` has a key other than `name`, `arguments`, `_meta` | `-32602` as above | param validation | unchanged (rule set merely widened by `_meta`) |
+| `params` has both `_meta` and another unknown key | `-32602` | param validation | unchanged consequence; accepting `_meta` does not relax others (spec edge case 1) |
+| `_meta` present but not an object (string / number / boolean / list / **null**) | `-32602` | param validation | **new** (FR-004) |
+| Tool `arguments` attempt identity override (e.g. `{"host": ...}`) | `result` with `"isError":true` and the standard failure text | tool dispatch guard | unchanged (FR-005); wins over a co-present valid `_meta` |
+| Frame > 32 KiB | `-32600` + connection end | framing | unchanged (FR-006) |
+| Missing/malformed `name` or `arguments` | existing handling | dispatch | unchanged (no new exceptions added) |
+
+Error envelope shape (unchanged): `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<request id or null>,"error":{"code":-326xx,"message":"..."}}`.
+
+## Distribution contract
+
+`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py` and
+`plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py` MUST remain byte-for-byte identical
+(SHA-256 equal). The codex companion has no separate test file; the main plugin's
+`test_task_handoff.py` is the single proof location and must contain at least one stdio test that
+drives a `tools/call` with an object-valued `_meta` through the real process and asserts dispatch
+(a `result` reply, not `-32602`) plus the absence of regression in the rejection table above.
