+# Phase 1 Data Model: Task-Handoff MCP Server Accepts Standard Client Metadata
+
+**Feature**: specs/001-bench/spec.md · **Date**: 2026-10-26
+
+The feature adds no persisted structures. Its "data model" is the set of request/response shapes
+validated on the wire and the invariants the two distributed files must satisfy. Entities below
+mirror the spec's Key Entities section.
+
+## Entity 1 — Tool-call request frame
+
+One newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 message read from the server's standard input.
+
+### Fields
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Rules |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `jsonrpc` | string | yes (frame) | Must equal `"2.0"`, else the frame is an invalid request. |
+| `id` | JSON value | yes (for responses) | Absent only for notifications, which are handled separately and unchanged by this feature. |
+| `method` | string | yes (frame) | `tools/call` is the method this feature changes; `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list` keep today's handling exactly. |
+| `params` | object | yes (for `tools/call`) | Validated below. |
+| `params.name` | string | yes (semantics unchanged) | Must name one of `offer`, `receive`, `status`; existing handling untouched. |
+| `params.arguments` | object \| null | no | Existing per-tool field allow-lists and required-field rules untouched. |
+| `params._meta` | object | **new: optional** | If present, MUST be a JSON object (`{...}`); any other type — string, number, boolean, list, **null** — is rejected. Contents are opaque: never selected, validated, consumed, or echoed. Bounded only by the whole-frame limit. |
+
+### Validation order for `tools/call` (post-change, all before dispatch, no side effects)
+
+1. Frame length ≤ `MAX_MCP_MESSAGE` (32 KiB) including its newline; oversized frames yield
+   `-32600` and terminate the connection — unchanged.
+2. Frame parses as a JSON object with `jsonrpc == "2.0"`, string `method`.
+3. `params` is an object.
+4. `set(params) ⊆ {"name", "arguments", "_meta"}` — any other key is rejected. **(changed: was
+   `{"name", "arguments"}`)**
+5. `"_meta" in params ⇒ isinstance(params["_meta"], dict)` — membership test required because
+   explicit `null` must be rejected but `.get("_meta")` conflates missing with null. **(new)**
+6. Dispatch to `_mcp_tool_call(name, arguments, host, session)` — `_meta` is not passed; the
+   dispatch signature is unchanged, which structurally enforces FR-002 (metadata cannot influence
+   tool selection, identities, or results).
+
+Rejection at steps 3–5 produces JSON-RPC error `-32602` ("invalid request") for the frame's id,
+with zero Runtime HTTP requests made (the observable "no runtime side effects" criterion).
+
+### State transitions
+
+```
+frame received ──(valid params incl. object _meta)──▶ dispatched: tools/call result envelope
+      │
+      ├──(_meta present, non-object / other unknown field / non-object params)──▶ -32602, connection continues
+      └──(oversized frame)──────────────────────────────────────────────────────▶ -32600, connection ends
+```
+
+## Entity 2 — Server session identity
+
+Held by the server process, supplied at startup, **never** by callers.
+
+| Component | Source | Rule enforced |
+|---|---|---|
+| Host | env `GRAPHHELM_MCP_HOST`, validated against `PORTABLE_HOST` before the serve loop starts | Unchanged by this feature. |
+| Session | env `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID`, validated against `ID`; must match `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` when re-checked inside tool phases | Unchanged. |
+| Identity-override refusal | `_mcp_tool_call` rejects tool `arguments` containing any field outside the per-tool allow-list (e.g. `host`, `sessionId`) → tool-level `isError: true` result | Unchanged (FR-005). A frame carrying both a valid `_meta` object and an override still hits this refusal first-in-precedence after param validation passes. |
+
+## Entity 3 — Distributed adapter copies
+
+Two physical file copies forming a distribution contract independent of behavior.
+
+| Copy | Path | Invariant |
+|---|---|---|
+| Main plugin | `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py` | Byte-for-byte identical to the twin (FR-007). |
+| Codex companion | `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py` | Byte-for-byte identical to the main copy (FR-007). |
+
+Verified pre-state: identical (27 443 bytes each). Post-change proof: byte/hash comparison in
+[quickstart.md](quickstart.md), step 2. The companion ships no separate test file (spec assumption),
+so byte identity is the entire consistency contract between the two plugins; behavioral proof lives
+in the main plugin's `test_task_handoff.py` (FR-008).
+
+## Relations
+
+```
+tool-call request frame ──validated against──▶ rules of §Entity 1
+        │ dispatches with (host, session) held by
+        ▼
+server session identity ◀──protected by── identity-override refusal (arguments allow-list)
+        │ served as file bytes from
+        ▼
+distributed adapter copies (byte-equal pair) ──exercised by── plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py
+```
+
+No state is stored between frames other than what the process already holds (identity, binding);
+adding `_meta` changes neither.
