+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately.
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Conceptually after Phase 1 (baseline noted). BLOCKS all user stories (fixes the single edit site).
+- **User Stories (Phases 3–5)**: US1 after Foundational. US2 after US1 (its type check needs the widened set). US3 after US1+US2 (the twin sync mirrors the complete fix).
+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: After all desired user stories are complete.
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: Starts after Foundational. No dependency on other stories. (T003 → T004.)
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Depends on US1's implementation T004 (the widened set must admit `_meta` before the non-object type check can be the discriminator). (T005, T006 → T007 → T008.)
+- **User Story 3 (P3)**: Depends on US1 (T004) and US2 (T007) so the synced twin carries the COMPLETE fix. (T009 → T010; T011 depends on all of the above.)
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written and shown to FAIL (RED) before the implementation task that turns them GREEN.
+- US1: T003 (test, RED) → T004 (impl, GREEN).
+- US2: T005, T006 (tests, RED) → T007 (impl, GREEN) → T008 (verify neighbors unchanged).
+- US3: mechanical mirror + byte verification, then the whole-suite green run.
+
+### Parallel Opportunities (honest — limited by file concentration)
+
+Nearly all of this feature concentrates in one adapter file and one test file, so true parallelism is limited; [P] is marked only where tasks touch different files with no mutual dependency.
+
+- **T012 and T013 (Polish)**: different activities on the finished change — T012 statically reviews the diff, T013 executes the validation — and can proceed together.
+- **Per-file staffing (not a [P] flag)**: the adapter file (`task_handoff.py`) serializes its own edits (T004 then T007), and the test file (`test_task_handoff.py`) serializes its own (T003 then T005/T006). Because these are DIFFERENT files, two engineers could work them concurrently and converge at each suite run.
+- **Cross-story staffing after T002**: US1's test task and US1's impl task are in different files and could be staffed in parallel, converging at T004's run; however for strict RED-first ordering, run T003 and observe RED before starting T004.
+- US2's T005 and T006 share the SAME test file, so they are NOT flagged [P] (conservative per the different-files rule).
