+## Notes
+
+- The `[P]` marker means different files with no dependency; it is used sparingly here because the change concentrates in two source files plus one test file.
+- `[Story]` labels (US1/US2/US3) give per-story traceability; Setup, Foundational, and Polish phases carry none.
+- Three files change in total (matching plan.md): the main adapter, its byte-identical twin, and the test file. No Rust crate, schema, CLI, or manifest is touched; no new dependencies, imports, modules, or public surface.
+- `_meta` is opaque throughout (FR-002): admitted iff present-and-object, never read after validation, never echoed; enforced structurally because the `_mcp_tool_call(...)` dispatch signature is left unchanged.
+- Commit after each task or logical group; stop at any checkpoint to validate the story independently. Avoid vague tasks, same-file conflicts, and cross-story dependencies that break independence.
